            <ArticleTitle>Pathology mimicking distal intestinal obstruction syndrome in cystic fibrosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>540-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Eight patients with cystic fibrosis had chronic abdominal pain and the other features of distal intestinal obstruction syndrome. Coexistent abdominal pathology was shown in six patients. Two had a small bowel volvulus, and the others had Crohn's disease, a small bowel fistula, appendix abscess, and an ovarian dermoid. Opiate abuse exacerbated symptoms in two other patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
